          en: '$\\mathrm{Cg}(x,y)$ intersects all congruences containing $(x,y)$, so $\\mathrm{Cg}(x,y)\\le \\theta$ iff $x\\mathrel{\\theta} y$. Swapping the pair preserves this intersection, and the bottom congruence is equality. The join containing $(x,z)$ and $(z,y)$ contains $(x,y)$ by transitivity. If $a\\nleq b$, some pair belongs to $e(a)$ but not $e(b)$; its principal congruence lies below $e(a)$ but not $e(b)$. Applying $e^{-1}$ gives the four color properties.',
